@startuml
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif
skinparam ArrowColor #3F5E52
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #AFC2B9
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #F7FAF8
skinparam SequenceLifeLineBorderColor #AFC2B9
skinparam SequenceLifeLineBackgroundColor #F7FAF8

title First-run credentials and WhatsApp pairing

autonumber
actor Operator
participant "React dashboard" as UI
participant "Express /app" as App
participant "Express /whatsapp" as WaRoutes
database "/app/data/wago.db" as Database
participant "Baileys client" as Baileys
database "/app/data/auth/" as Auth
participant "WhatsApp Web" as WhatsApp

Operator -> UI : Open Wago dashboard over HTTPS
UI -> App : GET /app/info
App --> UI : app/auth/setup state

alt Fresh gateway: no API key or hash exists
  Operator -> UI : Click Pair WhatsApp
  UI -> UI : Generate wa_<random> API-key candidate
  UI -> App : POST /app/bootstrap { apiKey }\nProduction Origin must use HTTPS\nand Origin host must match request Host
  App -> Database : Persist appId + SHA-256 API-key hash\n(raw generated key is not persisted)
  App --> UI : 201 appId + raw API key\nSet HttpOnly auth cookie
  UI -> UI : Keep raw key in sessionStorage
else Existing gateway credentials
  Operator -> UI : Enter existing API key
  UI -> UI : Store key in sessionStorage
  UI -> App : GET /app/info\nAuthorization: Bearer <API_KEY>
  App --> UI : authenticated=true
end

UI -> WaRoutes : POST /whatsapp/pair
WaRoutes -> Baileys : pairWhatsApp()
Baileys -> Baileys : Resolve current WA Web version
note right of Baileys
  Cache successful live version.
  If lookup fails, continue with
  Baileys bundled/default version.
end note
Baileys -> Auth : Read/write Baileys auth state
Baileys -> WhatsApp : Start linked-device session
WhatsApp --> Baileys : QR payload
Baileys --> WaRoutes : status=qr
WaRoutes --> UI : Pairing status
UI -> WaRoutes : GET /whatsapp/qr/image
WaRoutes --> UI : SVG QR
Operator -> WhatsApp : Scan QR from Linked devices
WhatsApp --> Baileys : connection=open
Baileys -> Database : Persist normalized account binding
UI -> WaRoutes : GET /whatsapp/status
WaRoutes --> UI : connected + binding + account health
@enduml
